elacao Sinal-Ruido' (Signal-to-Noise Ratio - SNR) [Data: Entities (1594, 1595); Relationships (2130, 2133)]. A higher SNR generally indicates better signal quality and fewer errors [Data: Entities (1601, 1595, 1594); Relationships (2137, 2130)]. The 'Grafico de Taxa de Erro de Bits (BER) VS. Relacao Sinal-Ruido (SNR)' visualizes this relationship [Data: Entities (1593); Relationships (2125)]. Different modulation schemes, such as BPSK and QAM256, are used in data transmission, each having different SNR requirements for a given BER [Data: Entities (1596, 1598); Relationships (2131, 2132)]. For instance, BPSK requires a lower SNR than QAM256 for the same error rate [Data: Relationships (2131, 2132)]. The distance limit for horizontal cabling in wired networks is also mentioned as a measure to help avoid signal attenuation and noise issues [Data: Entities (2046, 1562, 2031, 2057, 2802, 2796); Relationships (2777, 2802, 2796)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity is rated moderately high due to the critical nature of network connectivity in modern society and the potential vulnerabilities inherent in wireless technologies.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "STOP"}}], "created": 1787751142, "model": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": "default", "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1969, "prompt_tokens": 7284, "total_tokens": 9253, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "image_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 6783, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost": 0.00090553, "is